4.6 Walkthrough Using a Real Output of pmap -x 7714 (Hinglish)
Tumhare pmap -x 7714 output mein 6 columns hain. Inhe ek-ek karke tumhare actual output ke examples se samajhte hain, taaki tum khud bhi samajh sako aur end users ko bhi padha sako.
1. Address: memory region kahan start hota hai?
Example:
00005ddafa875000


Ye process ke virtual address space mein ek memory region ka starting address hai.
Jaise kisi ghar ka postal address hota hai, waise hi process ke virtual memory regions ke addresses hote hain. Operating system in addresses ka use memory ko locate aur manage karne ke liye karta hai.
Har row ek memory mapping dikhati hai.
Alag regions ke alag starting addresses ho sakte hain.
Ye physical RAM ka direct address zaroori nahi hai.
End user ko bolo: Address batata hai ki process ki virtual memory mein ye region kahan se start hota hai.
2. Kbytes: memory region kitna bada hai?
Tumhare output mein:
Address           Kbytes
00005ddafa875000       4
000076ec1b228000    1632


Iska matlab:
Pehla region 4 KB ka hai.
Doosra region 1632 KB ka hai.
Kbytes batata hai ki us particular mapping ka total size kitna hai. Ye sirf us row ka size hai, poore process ki memory nahi.
End user ko bolo: Agar Kbytes = 1632 hai, toh is mapping ka size 1632 KB hai. Ye zaroori nahi ki saari memory physical RAM mein loaded ho.
3. RSS: kitni memory physical RAM mein resident hai?
RSS ka full form Resident Set Size hai.
Tumhare output ka example:
Address           Kbytes    RSS
000076ec1b228000    1632    1056


Yahan:
Mapping ka total size = 1632 KB
Us mapping ka resident memory = 1056 KB
Matlab is mapping ke 1056 KB pages us waqt physical RAM mein resident the.
Baaki memory ke pages zaroori nahi ki us waqt RAM mein resident hon. RSS ko exact private memory mat samajhna, kyunki shared pages bhi RSS mein count ho sakte hain.
End user ko bolo: Kbytes mapping ka total size hai, jabki RSS batata hai ki us mapping ka kitna memory hissa physical RAM mein resident hai.
4. Dirty: kitni memory modified hui hai?
Example:
Kbytes    RSS    Dirty
4          4       4


Dirty modified memory pages ka size batata hai, jo clean state mein nahi hain relative to their backing storage.
Simple example: program ne writable memory mein koi value change ki. Us memory page ko dirty mark kiya ja sakta hai.
Lekin dhyan rahe, dirty memory ka matlab sirf ye nahi ki data disk par save nahi hua hai. Anonymous memory aur file-backed memory ke dirty pages ka behavior alag ho sakta hai.
Tumhare output mein Dirty = 0 ka matlab hai ki us mapping ke liye dirty memory report nahi hui.
End user ko bolo: Dirty column batata hai ki mapping mein kitni memory dirty count hui hai, yani modified memory pages se associated hai.
5. Mode: memory par kya operations allowed hain?
Tumhare output mein examples hain:
r----
r-x--
rw---


In letters ka meaning:
Symbol
Meaning
r
Read: memory ko padh sakte hain
w
Write: memory mein likh sakte hain
x
Execute: instructions execute kar sakte hain
-
Woh permission nahi hai


Examples:
r----: Read permission hai.
r-x--: Read aur execute permissions hain.
rw---: Read aur write permissions hain.
Ye permissions memory protection ka hissa hain. Inse operating system process ke memory regions ko alag-alag access rights de sakta hai.
End user ko bolo: Mode batata hai ki process us memory region ko read, write ya execute kar sakta hai ya nahi.
